.TH NAUSICAA 1 "November 2026" "Nausicaa 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nausicaa \- small video player for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nausicaa
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR|\fIPLAYLIST\fR|\fIURL\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nausicaa plays your videos, and nothing else. Files, folders, playlists
(.m3u, .m3u8, .xspf, .pls) and addresses given on the command line replace the
play queue and the first one is played. A single video brings the other videos
of its folder with it. If Nausicaa is already running, they are sent to the
running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-enqueue
Add to the play queue instead of replacing it.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nausicaa/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nausicaa/queue.json
The play queue, offered again on the welcome page.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nausicaa/positions.json
Where each video was left, to resume it.
.SH AUTHOR
Tof <nourpon@gmail.com>
